-- חוזר הממונה על השכר 2011-1-48 — תוספת מעונות (זכויות הוריות), על פי הסכם המסגרת מיום 12.1.2011 (7.8.2011)
-- The Wage Controller sets out the childcare supplement (parental rights)
-- under clause 11 of the framework agreement of 12.1.2011: who is entitled,
-- the monthly amounts from 1.9.2011 for up to two children under 5, part
-- time, the periods for which it is paid, its nature, and its replacing of
-- any other childcare arrangement for a child under 5.
--
-- Corpus note: the source lists its items with letters (א, ב, ג …) and the
-- corpus publishes them with digits, so the text's own references ("סעיף
-- 2א'", "סעיף 3 א'", "סעיף 3 ב'") name labels the published page does not
-- show; and the source's second heading numbered 3 ("החלפה/ביטול הסדר
-- מעונות אחר") is published as a paragraph inside item 8, with its items
-- nested under the payment section. Comments below give the source's
-- letters.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common
IMPORT conventions

§ `תוספת מעונות (זכויות הוריות) 2011-1-48`

-- akn:preamble/p1 The letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The letterhead's address line; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p3 The Hebrew date; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 The date, 7.8.2011; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 The circular's number, הע-2011-1-48; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p6 The addressee (the Senior Deputy Accountant-General); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p7 The subject line; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p1 The reference line: the circular that sent out the framework agreement (הע-2011-1-10); no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p2 The heading of section 1, "general"; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p3 Background: the framework agreement of 12.1.2011 and its clause 11 on the supplement, sent out with the earlier circular; the rules follow.
-- akn:hc_1/p4 The heading of section 2, "applicability"; its items follow.

@desc A month of a public-sector employee's employment, as far as the childcare supplement asks about it.
DECLARE `employee month` HAS
    `employed by an employer that signed the agreement`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc graded in one of the gradings the New General Histadrut represents, with salary computed by collective agreements (section 2א(2))
    `parent status`                  IS A `parent status`
    `children under 5`               IS A NUMBER  @desc the employee's children who have not yet turned 5 (for a widower or divorcé: those in his custody)
    `position fraction`              IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position held (1 = full)
    `entitled to salary from the employer and at its expense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc false for a period of national-insurance maternity pay or of unpaid leave (section 3ז)

DECLARE `parent status` IS ONE OF
    `a mother`
    `a widower or divorcé with the children in his custody`
    `a father the Equal Employment Opportunities Law entitles` @desc a father to whom section 4(a) of the Equal Employment Opportunities Law, 1988, extends a parenting right; the law is applied, not restated, here (section 2ג)
    `another employee`

DECLARE `childcare supplement action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the childcare supplement` HAS `childcare amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `demand receipts for the childcare costs`

§§ `2 תחולת תשלום תוספת מעונות`

-- 2א: the supplement applies to every employee who meets all of: (1)
-- employed by an employer that signed the agreement, (2) graded in a
-- grading the New General Histadrut represents, salary by collective
-- agreements, (3) a mother of a child or children not yet 5.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_2 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_3
GIVEN e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement applies to a mother` e IF
        e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement`
    AND e's `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements`
    AND e's `parent status` EQUALS `a mother`
    AND e's `children under 5` AT LEAST 1

-- 2ב: a widower or divorcé with a child in his custody is treated as a
-- female employee, subject to 2א: its conditions (1) and (2), and a child
-- not yet 5 (in his custody).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2
GIVEN e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement applies to a widower or divorcé` e IF
        e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement`
    AND e's `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements`
    AND e's `parent status` EQUALS `a widower or divorcé with the children in his custody`
    AND e's `children under 5` AT LEAST 1

-- 2ג: the supplement is a "right in connection with parenthood" under
-- section 4(b) of the Equal Employment Opportunities Law, and the law's
-- section 4(a) applies to it (as in chapter 35.1 of the Civil Service
-- Regulations, attached to the circular). Who section 4(a) admits is the
-- law's, an input here (the parent status); the conditions of 2א(1)–(2)
-- and a child not yet 5 still apply.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement is a right in connection with parenthood` IS TRUE

@ref akn:hc_1__para_3
GIVEN e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(a) of the law extends the supplement to the employee` e IF
        e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement`
    AND e's `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements`
    AND e's `parent status` EQUALS `a father the Equal Employment Opportunities Law entitles`
    AND e's `children under 5` AT LEAST 1

§§ `3 תשלום תוספת מעונות`

-- akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3 The heading of section 3, "paying the supplement"; its items follow.

-- From 1.9.2011 a reimbursement of the cost of keeping a child in a day
-- care centre ("תוספת מעונות") is paid as follows.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3/p2
`the supplement is paid from` MEANS Date 1 9 2011

-- The employer pays the supplement for the month; the circular sets a
-- monthly amount and no payment date, so it is read as due within the
-- month (time in months).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3/p2
GIVEN e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `childcare supplement action`
DECIDE `the employer pays the supplement` e IS
    IF `the monthly childcare supplement` e GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `pay the childcare supplement` paid
               PROVIDED paid AT LEAST `the monthly childcare supplement` e
         WITHIN 1
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "2011-1-48 section 3: the childcare supplement was not paid for the month"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 3א: it is paid as a partial participation in the cost of keeping a child
-- in a day care centre or other supervision, by the conditions that follow.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_1
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement is a partial participation in the cost of a day care centre or other supervision` IS TRUE

-- 3ב: paid to an employee who is a mother of a child, as in section 2
-- (which also admits a widower or divorcé and, by the law, a father) …
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_2
GIVEN e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the childcare supplement` e IF
        `the supplement applies to a mother` e
    OR  `the supplement applies to a widower or divorcé` e
    OR  `section 4(a) of the law extends the supplement to the employee` e

-- … and she is not required to bring the employer receipts (for
-- convenience). The text sets no time limit.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `childcare supplement action`
DECIDE `no receipts are demanded` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `demand receipts for the childcare costs`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "2011-1-48 section 3ב: the employee is not required to bring receipts"

-- 3ג: the amount for up to two children up to age 5: (1) one or a first
-- child, 300 shekels a month; (2) a second child, 200.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_3
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER @desc the children up to age 5 paid for (at most two, section 3ה)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-position amount for children` n IS
    BRANCH IF n AT LEAST 2 THEN `the monthly amount for one or a first child` PLUS `the monthly amount for a second child`
           IF n AT LEAST 1 THEN `the monthly amount for one or a first child`
           OTHERWISE 0

@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_3__pnt_1
`the monthly amount for one or a first child` MEANS 300

@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_3__pnt_2
`the monthly amount for a second child` MEANS 200

-- 3ד: the amount is for a full position; for a part-time position it is
-- computed by the part. (The text says "the amount stated below"; the
-- amounts are the ones stated above, in 3ג.) F-2011-08-07_sachar_2011-1-48_maonot-base-b:
-- a position above full is neither. Convention position.above-full
-- (conventions.toml): the full-position amount is pro rata to the position
-- above one too, as the text sets no ceiling.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_4
GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position share paid` f IS
    f

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position share on the other reading, capped at full` f IS
    min f 1

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `3ד decides the position` f IF
    f AT MOST 1

`3ד does not decide a position above full` MEANS
        (NOT (`3ד decides the position` 1.2))
    AND (NOT (`the position share paid` 1.2 EQUALS `the position share on the other reading, capped at full` 1.2))
#ASSERT `3ד does not decide a position above full`

-- 3ה: paid at the same time for up to two children; nothing for any
-- further child of the same mother under 5.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_5
GIVEN e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `children paid for` e IS
    min (e's `children under 5`) 2

-- 3ו: updated once a year, in January, as the agreement of 12.1.2011
-- details; the updated amounts are published in the Wage Controller's
-- circulars. Until the first update the amounts here apply; after it, the
-- amounts in force are an input from those circulars.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_6
GIVEN `month` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the amounts are updated in the month` `month` IF
    DATE_MONTH `month` EQUALS 1

@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_6
GIVEN `month` IS A DATE, `first update` IS A DATE @desc 1 January of the first yearly update, published in a later circular of the Wage Controller
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this circular's amounts are in force` `month` `first update` IF
        `month` AT LEAST `the supplement is paid from`
    AND `month` LESS THAN `first update`

-- 3ז: paid only for a period in which the employee is entitled to salary
-- from the employer and at its expense — not, for example, for a period of
-- national-insurance maternity pay or of unpaid leave.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_7
GIVEN e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the month is one the supplement is paid for` e IF
    e's `entitled to salary from the employer and at its expense`

-- 3ח: a reimbursement of expenses, not salary for any purpose; the
-- employer makes for it the provisions it makes for an expense
-- reimbursement.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_8
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement is salary` IS FALSE

@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_8
GIVEN `the employer's provisions for an expense reimbursement` IS A NUMBER @desc the contributions the employer's practice makes for an expense-reimbursement component; not set here
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `provisions made for the supplement` `the employer's provisions for an expense reimbursement` IS
    `the employer's provisions for an expense reimbursement`

§§ `3 The supplement for a month, put together`

@export default The monthly childcare supplement (in shekels) at this circular's amounts, for a month from 1.9.2011 until the first yearly update
GIVEN e IS AN `employee month` @desc the employee and the month
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly childcare supplement` e IS
    IF `entitled to the childcare supplement` e AND `the month is one the supplement is paid for` e
    THEN `the full-position amount for children` (`children paid for` e) TIMES `the position share paid` (e's `position fraction`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `3 החלפה/ביטול הסדר מעונות אחר`

-- akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_8/p2 The heading of the second section numbered 3, "replacing or cancelling another childcare arrangement", which the corpus publishes inside item 8; its items follow.

@desc An arrangement other than this circular's for childcare costs.
DECLARE `other childcare arrangement` HAS
    `for a child under 5`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `a general arrangement`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc set at the level of the grading, the employer, the workplace or the work area, not for the individual employee
    `pays another benefit towards childcare` IS A BOOLEAN
    `monthly benefit for one or a first child` IS A NUMBER
    `monthly benefit for two or more children` IS A NUMBER

-- 3א (second 3): from the September 2011 salary, the supplement replaces
-- and cancels every other arrangement for a child under 5, whatever it is
-- called — direct reimbursement or any other benefit, direct or indirect,
-- funding, subsidy or a discount on the cost.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_9
GIVEN a IS AN `other childcare arrangement`, `month` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement replaces and cancels the other arrangement` a `month` IF
        a's `for a child under 5`
    AND `month` AT LEAST Date 1 9 2011

-- 3ב (second 3): "the stated in section 3 א' above" does not apply where a
-- general arrangement (at the level of the grading, the employer, the
-- workplace or the work area) meets all of: (1) it pays another benefit
-- towards the cost of a day care centre or other supervision; (2) that
-- benefit is more than 300 a month for one or a first child AND more than
-- 500 for two or more.
-- F-2011-08-07_sachar_2011-1-48_maonot-a: two sections are numbered 3, so
-- "section 3 א'" names either one.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_10 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_10__pnt_1 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_10__pnt_2
GIVEN a IS AN `other childcare arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the general arrangement is kept` a IF
        a's `a general arrangement`
    AND a's `pays another benefit towards childcare`
    AND (a's `monthly benefit for one or a first child` `is above` 300)
    AND (a's `monthly benefit for two or more children` `is above` 500)

-- The two readings of "section 3 א'" for a kept general arrangement:
-- read as the payment section's item א (the supplement is paid), the
-- supplement is not paid; read as this section's item א (the replacing),
-- only the cancelling is lifted, and nothing in the text stops the
-- supplement too. The reading adopted is the first outcome: the general
-- arrangement instead of the supplement, as item ג's "subject to 3 ב'"
-- and ב's own "the general arrangement continues to apply" describe.
DECLARE `reading of section 3 א'` IS ONE OF
    `the payment section's item א`
    `the replacing section's item א`

GIVEN r IS A `reading of section 3 א'`, a IS AN `other childcare arrangement`, e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement beside the arrangement under` r a e IS
    IF `the general arrangement is kept` a
    THEN CONSIDER r
         WHEN `the payment section's item א` THEN 0
         WHEN `the replacing section's item א` THEN `the monthly childcare supplement` e
    ELSE `the monthly childcare supplement` e

GIVEN a IS AN `other childcare arrangement`, e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement beside the arrangement` a e IS
    `the supplement beside the arrangement under` `the payment section's item א` a e

-- In such a case the general arrangement continues to apply, by its own
-- provisions and eligibility rules; whether the conditions hold is judged
-- at the general level, not per employee. For employers under section 29
-- of the Budget Foundations Law, 1985, this is subject to that section.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_10__pnt_2/p2 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_10__pnt_2/p3
GIVEN a IS AN `other childcare arrangement`, `month` IS A DATE, `section 29 permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc for an employer under section 29 of the Budget Foundations Law, 1985: whether that section permits the arrangement; TRUE for any other employer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other arrangement survives` a `month` `section 29 permits it` IF
        (NOT `the supplement replaces and cancels the other arrangement` a `month`)
    OR  (`the general arrangement is kept` a AND `section 29 permits it`)

-- 3ג (second 3): for gradings or employers with an arrangement for a child
-- of 5 or over, the arrangement in force when the agreement was signed
-- continues for those ages, provided no arrangement is doubled; for a child
-- up to 5 this circular applies, subject to 3ב; for employers under section
-- 29 of the Budget Foundations Law, subject to that section.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3__cls_11
GIVEN `child is 5 or over` IS A BOOLEAN, `an arrangement for that age existed when the agreement was signed` IS A BOOLEAN, `it would double an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN, `section 29 permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc for an employer under section 29 of the Budget Foundations Law, 1985: whether that section permits the arrangement; TRUE for any other employer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the existing arrangement applies to the child` `child is 5 or over` `an arrangement for that age existed when the agreement was signed` `it would double an arrangement` `section 29 permits it` IF
        `child is 5 or over`
    AND `an arrangement for that age existed when the agreement was signed`
    AND (NOT `it would double an arrangement`)
    AND `section 29 permits it`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off (the Wage Controller), the copies list, the internal number and the letterhead's footer; no rule.

§§ `Findings`

`the sections numbered 3` MEANS
    LIST "תשלום תוספת מעונות", "החלפה/ביטול הסדר מעונות אחר"


`a mother of two in a full position` MEANS
    `employee month` WITH
        `employed by an employer that signed the agreement` IS TRUE
        `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements` IS TRUE
        `parent status`                IS `a mother`
        `children under 5`             IS 2
        `position fraction`            IS 1
        `entitled to salary from the employer and at its expense` IS TRUE

`a better general arrangement` MEANS
    `other childcare arrangement` WITH
        `for a child under 5`           IS TRUE
        `a general arrangement`         IS TRUE
        `pays another benefit towards childcare` IS TRUE
        `monthly benefit for one or a first child` IS 350
        `monthly benefit for two or more children` IS 550

-- F-2011-08-07_sachar_2011-1-48_maonot-a.
`two sections are numbered 3 and the readings of 3 א' differ` MEANS
        count `the sections numbered 3` EQUALS 2
    AND NOT (`the supplement beside the arrangement under` `the payment section's item א` `a better general arrangement` `a mother of two in a full position`
             EQUALS `the supplement beside the arrangement under` `the replacing section's item א` `a better general arrangement` `a mother of two in a full position`)
#ASSERT `two sections are numbered 3 and the readings of 3 א' differ`

§§ `Worked examples`

`a mother of three at half a position` MEANS
    `employee month` WITH
        `employed by an employer that signed the agreement` IS TRUE
        `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements` IS TRUE
        `parent status`                IS `a mother`
        `children under 5`             IS 3
        `position fraction`            IS 0.5
        `entitled to salary from the employer and at its expense` IS TRUE

`a divorced father of one` MEANS
    `employee month` WITH
        `employed by an employer that signed the agreement` IS TRUE
        `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements` IS TRUE
        `parent status`                IS `a widower or divorcé with the children in his custody`
        `children under 5`             IS 1
        `position fraction`            IS 1
        `entitled to salary from the employer and at its expense` IS TRUE

`a mother of one on maternity pay` MEANS
    `employee month` WITH
        `employed by an employer that signed the agreement` IS TRUE
        `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements` IS TRUE
        `parent status`                IS `a mother`
        `children under 5`             IS 1
        `position fraction`            IS 1
        `entitled to salary from the employer and at its expense` IS FALSE

`a married father of one` MEANS
    `employee month` WITH
        `employed by an employer that signed the agreement` IS TRUE
        `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements` IS TRUE
        `parent status`                IS `another employee`
        `children under 5`             IS 1
        `position fraction`            IS 1
        `entitled to salary from the employer and at its expense` IS TRUE

`a mother of one at 120%` MEANS
    `employee month` WITH
        `employed by an employer that signed the agreement` IS TRUE
        `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements` IS TRUE
        `parent status`                IS `a mother`
        `children under 5`             IS 1
        `position fraction`            IS 1.2
        `entitled to salary from the employer and at its expense` IS TRUE

`a smaller general arrangement` MEANS
    `other childcare arrangement` WITH
        `for a child under 5`           IS TRUE
        `a general arrangement`         IS TRUE
        `pays another benefit towards childcare` IS TRUE
        `monthly benefit for one or a first child` IS 350
        `monthly benefit for two or more children` IS 450

#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement` `a mother of two in a full position` EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement` `a mother of three at half a position` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement` `a divorced father of one` EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement` `a mother of one on maternity pay` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement` `a married father of one` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement` `a mother of one at 120%` EQUALS 360
#ASSERT `the general arrangement is kept` `a better general arrangement`
#ASSERT NOT `the general arrangement is kept` `a smaller general arrangement`
#ASSERT `the other arrangement survives` `a better general arrangement` (Date 1 10 2011) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the other arrangement survives` `a smaller general arrangement` (Date 1 10 2011) TRUE
#ASSERT `the other arrangement survives` `a smaller general arrangement` (Date 1 8 2011) TRUE
#ASSERT `the supplement beside the arrangement` `a better general arrangement` `a mother of two in a full position` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the supplement beside the arrangement` `a smaller general arrangement` `a mother of two in a full position` EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `this circular's amounts are in force` (Date 15 12 2011) (Date 1 1 2012)
#ASSERT NOT `this circular's amounts are in force` (Date 15 8 2011) (Date 1 1 2012)

#TRACE `the employer pays the supplement` `a mother of two in a full position` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the childcare supplement` 500 AT 0
#TRACE `no receipts are demanded` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `demand receipts for the childcare costs` AT 0

§§ `Property checks`

-- The circular's rules over their whole finite space: every parent
-- status, 0 to 4 children under 5, positions of 0, a half, one and 1.2,
-- each of the three yes-or-no conditions (an employer that signed, a
-- Histadrut grading, salary from the employer), every general arrangement
-- paying 250, 300, 301 or 350 for one child and 450, 500, 501 or 550 for
-- two, and the days the circular names and the day before each.

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE
`every parent status` MEANS LIST `a mother`, `a widower or divorcé with the children in his custody`, `a father the Equal Employment Opportunities Law entitles`, `another employee`
`the positions checked` MEANS LIST 0, 0.5, 1, 1.2

GIVEN s IS A `parent status`, n IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER, a IS A BOOLEAN, g IS A BOOLEAN, w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `employee month`
DECIDE `a checked month` s n f a g w IS
    `employee month` WITH
        `employed by an employer that signed the agreement` IS a
        `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements` IS g
        `parent status`                IS s
        `children under 5`             IS n
        `position fraction`            IS f
        `entitled to salary from the employer and at its expense` IS w

GIVEN p IS A FUNCTION FROM `employee month` TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds for every checked month` p IF
    all (GIVEN s YIELD
            all (GIVEN n YIELD
                    all (GIVEN f YIELD
                            all (GIVEN a YIELD
                                    all (GIVEN g YIELD
                                            all (GIVEN w YIELD p (`a checked month` s n f a g w))
                                                `both booleans`)
                                        `both booleans`)
                                `both booleans`)
                        `the positions checked`)
                (range 0 4))
        `every parent status`

-- 2א, 2ב, 2ג: at most one of the three routes admits an employee, and
-- together they admit exactly an employee of a signing employer, in a
-- Histadrut grading, with a child under 5, who is a mother, a widower or
-- divorcé with custody, or a father the law entitles.
GIVEN e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `routes that admit` e IS
    count (filter id (LIST `the supplement applies to a mother` e,
                           `the supplement applies to a widower or divorcé` e,
                           `section 4(a) of the law extends the supplement to the employee` e))

GIVEN e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the routes admit exactly the employees section 2 names, each by one route` e IF
        `routes that admit` e AT MOST 1
    AND `entitled to the childcare supplement` e
        EQUALS (    e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement`
                AND e's `graded in a Histadrut-represented grading paid by collective agreements`
                AND e's `children under 5` AT LEAST 1
                AND NOT (e's `parent status` EQUALS `another employee`))
#ASSERT `holds for every checked month` `the routes admit exactly the employees section 2 names, each by one route`

-- 3ג-3ז: the supplement is never negative and never above 300 + 200 for
-- each full position held; it
-- is nothing in a month without salary from the employer; a third or later
-- child adds nothing; and it never falls with more children or with a
-- larger position.
GIVEN e IS AN `employee month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement is within 0 and 500, nothing without salary, for at most two children` e IF
        `the monthly childcare supplement` e AT LEAST 0
    AND `the monthly childcare supplement` e AT MOST (`the monthly amount for one or a first child` PLUS `the monthly amount for a second child`) TIMES max 1 (e's `position fraction`)
    AND (e's `entitled to salary from the employer and at its expense` OR `the monthly childcare supplement` e EQUALS 0)
    AND `children paid for` e AT MOST 2
#ASSERT `holds for every checked month` `the supplement is within 0 and 500, nothing without salary, for at most two children`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN s YIELD
                all (GIVEN n YIELD
                        all (GIVEN f YIELD
                                    `the monthly childcare supplement` (`a checked month` s n f TRUE TRUE TRUE)
                                    AT MOST `the monthly childcare supplement` (`a checked month` s (n PLUS 1) f TRUE TRUE TRUE)
                                AND `the monthly childcare supplement` (`a checked month` s n f TRUE TRUE TRUE)
                                    AT MOST `the monthly childcare supplement` (`a checked month` s n (f PLUS 0.5) TRUE TRUE TRUE))
                            `the positions checked`)
                    (range 0 4))
            `every parent status`

-- 3 and 3ו: the circular's amounts run from 1.9.2011, not the day before,
-- until the first yearly update (a January 1, here 1.1.2012) and not on it.
`the circular's amounts run from 1.9.2011 to the first update` MEANS
        `this circular's amounts are in force` (Date 1 9 2011) (Date 1 1 2012)
    AND NOT `this circular's amounts are in force` (Date 31 8 2011) (Date 1 1 2012)
    AND `this circular's amounts are in force` (Date 31 12 2011) (Date 1 1 2012)
    AND NOT `this circular's amounts are in force` (Date 1 1 2012) (Date 1 1 2012)
    AND `the amounts are updated in the month` (Date 1 1 2012)
    AND NOT `the amounts are updated in the month` (Date 31 12 2011)
#ASSERT `the circular's amounts run from 1.9.2011 to the first update`

`every benefit for one child`  MEANS LIST 250, 300, 301, 350
`every benefit for two children` MEANS LIST 450, 500, 501, 550

GIVEN u IS A BOOLEAN, `general` IS A BOOLEAN, `pays` IS A BOOLEAN, b1 IS A NUMBER, b2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `other childcare arrangement`
DECIDE `a checked arrangement` u `general` `pays` b1 b2 IS
    `other childcare arrangement` WITH
        `for a child under 5`           IS u
        `a general arrangement`         IS `general`
        `pays another benefit towards childcare` IS `pays`
        `monthly benefit for one or a first child` IS b1
        `monthly benefit for two or more children` IS b2

GIVEN p IS A FUNCTION FROM `other childcare arrangement` TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds for every checked arrangement` p IF
    all (GIVEN u YIELD
            all (GIVEN `general` YIELD
                    all (GIVEN `pays` YIELD
                            all (GIVEN b1 YIELD
                                    all (GIVEN b2 YIELD p (`a checked arrangement` u `general` `pays` b1 b2))
                                        `every benefit for two children`)
                                `every benefit for one child`)
                        `both booleans`)
                `both booleans`)
        `both booleans`

-- The arrangement's benefit for a mother of n children: the one-child
-- figure for one, the two-or-more figure for more.
GIVEN a IS AN `other childcare arrangement`, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the arrangement's benefit for` a n IS
    IF n AT MOST 1
    THEN a's `monthly benefit for one or a first child`
    ELSE a's `monthly benefit for two or more children`

-- Second 3, items א and ב: an arrangement for a child under 5 survives
-- from 1.9.2011 exactly where it is kept (and section 29 permits it),
-- and every arrangement survives the day before. A kept arrangement is
-- kept exactly from more than 300 and more than 500, as 3ב(2) says, and
-- pays every full-time mother of 1 to 4 children more than the supplement
-- it displaces: 3ב's thresholds are this circular's own amounts.
GIVEN a IS AN `other childcare arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the replacing and keeping are as the second section 3 says` a IF
        `the general arrangement is kept` a
        EQUALS (    a's `a general arrangement`
                AND a's `pays another benefit towards childcare`
                AND a's `monthly benefit for one or a first child` AT LEAST 301
                AND a's `monthly benefit for two or more children` AT LEAST 501)
    AND all (GIVEN s29 YIELD
                    `the other arrangement survives` a (Date 31 8 2011) s29
                AND `the other arrangement survives` a (Date 1 9 2011) s29
                    EQUALS ((NOT a's `for a child under 5`) OR (`the general arrangement is kept` a AND s29)))
            `both booleans`
    AND ((NOT `the general arrangement is kept` a)
         OR all (GIVEN n YIELD `the arrangement's benefit for` a n GREATER THAN `the monthly childcare supplement` (`a checked month` `a mother` n 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE))
                (range 1 4))
#ASSERT `holds for every checked arrangement` `the replacing and keeping are as the second section 3 says`

-- F-2011-08-07_sachar_2011-1-48_maonot-base-a over every arrangement and
-- every full-time mother of 0 to 4 children, with and without salary: the
-- two readings of "section 3 א'" part exactly where the arrangement is
-- kept and a supplement is due.
GIVEN a IS AN `other childcare arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the readings of 3 א' part exactly where a kept arrangement meets a supplement due` a IF
    all (GIVEN n YIELD
            all (GIVEN w YIELD
                    LET e MEANS `a checked month` `a mother` n 1 TRUE TRUE w
                    IN  (NOT (`the supplement beside the arrangement under` `the payment section's item א` a e
                              EQUALS `the supplement beside the arrangement under` `the replacing section's item א` a e))
                        EQUALS (`the general arrangement is kept` a AND `the monthly childcare supplement` e GREATER THAN 0))
                `both booleans`)
        (range 0 4)
#ASSERT `holds for every checked arrangement` `the readings of 3 א' part exactly where a kept arrangement meets a supplement due`

-- F-2011-08-07_sachar_2011-1-48_maonot-base-b over positions above full
-- from 1.05 to 1.5: 3ד decides none of them, the reading adopted pays each
-- pro rata, and the capped reading would pay each less.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN k YIELD
                LET f MEANS 1 PLUS k DIVIDED BY 20
                IN      NOT `3ד decides the position` f
                    AND `the position share paid` f EQUALS f
                    AND `the position share on the other reading, capped at full` f LESS THAN f)
            (range 1 10)
